    {
      "worldId": "offset-pan",
      "decision": "reject-local-low-surface-organization",
      "reason": "Two low sheets span nearly the entire bed, producing long straight gray/pink interfaces like pasted polygon panels. The low-grade same-angle view repeated this defect. Keep the first edge-owner, solid geometry and terrain; reduce only the second and third relief sheets to short exposures adjoining their respective solid shoulder and real bank."
    },
    {
      "worldId": "thin-delta",
      "decision": "reject-ground-edge-profile",
      "reason": "The long bank repeats isolated pointed cells, resembling a fence. Fix continuous bank geometry rather than hide the rhythm with color/noise. The end views confirm only small near rims, not the entire shore."
    }
